<title>MOROCCO: Moroccan bank launches two investment firms.</title>
<headline>Moroccan bank launches two investment firms.</headline>
<dateline>RABAT 1997-01-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Morocco's Banque Marocaine du Commerce Exterieur said on Thursday it has set up two firms to attract public savings to be invested in shares on the Casablanca stock exchange and in state-backed bonds.</p>
<p>The companies, Irad and Sicavenir, will have initial capital of 5 million dirhams each ($5,747) and are to be listed on the Casablanca Bourse.</p>
<p>Shares will have a nominal value of 1,000 dirhams.</p>
<p>($1 = 8.7 dirhams)</p>
</text>
